00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.280
I'm going to go out on a limb and say yes.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:17.120
Uh, I think that that basic vibe, that, that basic feel from RC Pro-Am is there.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.320
Uh, I just have a soft spot for isometric games in the first place.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:29.240
And even though this game doesn't have like a, like a, the typical feel of a racer, like there's no accelerate button.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:32.660
It's just the direction you push is the direction you go.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:42.700
Yeah. But it also like, you have to take into account that the direction you push is also going to feel an amount of, uh, momentum.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:48.380
So it's also sort of like you're nudging it in that direction instead of actually going in that direction.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.940
It's kind of complex when you think about it, but when you actually push the buttons, it's very intuitive.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:57.980
Uh, it's just a little, you gotta get the hang of it is all.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:07.560
Yeah. And it's not like this hard to read, uh, 3D depth that we've seen with other games that try to do 3D because it's the isometric and we're kind of used to it at this point.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.240
Uh, it is, it is kind of like easy to tell when they're going to be turns.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.080
Uh, they're not just like sudden, uh, you know, all of a sudden a blinker on your left saying, okay, you're going to start turning left now.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.120
And then it's like a hard turn.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.180
Like we've seen in mock rider and games like that.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:35.140
I feel like visually the course, even when they do get more complicated with actual like gaps and obstacles in the course themselves, it's still a readable thing that makes it easy to, uh, understand how to, how to drive these things.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.680
You know, if you do have to take it slow or, or bank a turn or something like that.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:47.300
The interesting part of course comes not just from the racing, but the combat aspect because it's four ships racing at once and you can shoot your rival ships.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.920
You can destroy track obstacles.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:52.040
You have to jump over certain obstacles or pits.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:58.000
